  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In January 2025 remarks, Holyoak said AI has potential to benefit consumers and make American businesses more effective, and that the FTC should act circumspectly, promote competition and innovation, and avoid unclear regulations or misguided enforcement actions. In a September 2025 statement, she said AI could be a momentous driver of innovation and economic growth, and that the FTC is committed to giving AI the ability to develop while meeting its mandate to ensure competitive markets and protect consumers from unlawful conduct. She also expressed concern about reports that AI chatbots can engage in alarming interactions with young users and that companies offering generative AI companion chatbots might have been warned by their own employees about insufficient protections for young users.",
